# NetHack 5.0 configuration for the Nintendo 3DS port.
#
# This file is read from:  sdmc:/3ds/nethack/config/NetHack.cnf
# (a copy is placed there automatically the first time the game runs).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map display: tiles vs. characters
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   tiled_map    - draw the map on the top screen using graphical tiles
#   !tiled_map   - draw the map using traditional characters / symbols
#
# Leave exactly one of the next two lines uncommented.
OPTIONS=tiled_map
#OPTIONS=!tiled_map

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tile size (pixels).  Default is 16x16 when these are not set.
# The map shows as many tiles as fit on the 400x240 top screen, so larger
# tiles mean a smaller visible map area (the view scrolls with the hero).
# Smaller values give a wider view, larger values a more detailed one.
# In character mode the equivalent symbol size is set from the game's
# OPTIONS/SETTINGS screen (stored as char_width/char_height in 3dsui.cfg).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#OPTIONS=tile_width:16
#OPTIONS=tile_height:16

# You can also switch at any time from within the game:
#   press START, choose Settings, then open the "3DS UI settings" category.
# The same screen has a "NetHack settings" category for the common nethackrc
# options (tutorial prompt, status fields, autopickup, hints, and so on), and
# a "More prompts" row which can skip the --More-- keypress.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Controls
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D-pad moves the hero; the circle pad pans the map view (and moves the
# cursor while a look/glance command is active).  The soft keyboard's digit
# row uses number-pad directions (1 = down-left, 3 = down-right, ...).
# The port forces number_pad:1 so this always works, even with an old
# NetHack.cnf on the SD card; the line is here for documentation.
#OPTIONS=number_pad:1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sound
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Effects are on by default and play through the port's CSND backend.
# Own sounds can be dropped into sdmc:/3ds/nethack/sounds/<key>/0.wav
# (16-bit mono PCM WAV) without rebuilding; key names are listed in
# sys/3ds/README.md.  A deaf hero hears nothing, except footsteps.
#OPTIONS=!sounds
#OPTIONS=soundlib:sound3ds

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nice-to-have defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIONS=color
OPTIONS=hilite_pet
